Our solution will be deployed progressively, with a pilot phase on a limited perimeter followed by progressive generalisation to all services. Change-management support and staff training will be provided as part of our additional resources to ensure smooth adoption. Our joint steering committee and operational committee will oversee the project progress, and our single point of contact, the project director, will be responsible for coordinating the efforts and addressing any concerns or issues that may arise.

Throughout the 5-year timeframe, we will maintain a high level of availability (99.9%) and ensure response times compatible with daily clinical use (below 2 seconds for common queries). Our solution will integrate with the existing hospital information system (SIH) and electronic patient record (DPI), supporting health interoperability standards (HL7 / FHIR) and the national health identifier (INS). We will provide a high level of answer relevance, ensuring that our AI assistance tool effectively supports hospital staff in their daily activities.
